KWin: the cursor plane's atomic test skipped when only its position changed (6.7.5 port of patches/kwin/0062, 2026-10-18)

DrmPipeline::presentAsync tested the full state before every asynchronous cursor update, and a cursor
update is requested several times per pointer event: with a 4000 Hz mouse, thousands of atomic tests a
second. A main-line guest on virtio-gpu does the same (bench/ab/vm_cursor_tests_1018.sh: the 6.7.5
guest's KWin made 5,038 tests a second at 4000 Hz). Updates that change nothing are now dropped, and when
nothing but the position changed since the last successful test (same layer, buffer, source, size,
hotspot, transform, zpos, and the same crtc edges crossed, with 64 pixels or more of the plane visible),
that test is reused. Every other test or commit of the pipeline, a pending-state change and a failed
commit in the commit thread reset it. KWIN_CURSOR_TEST_EVERY_MOVE=1 restores the previous behaviour; =2
drops unchanged updates but tests every other one; $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-cursor-test-every-move holding
0, 1 or 2 overrides the variable while it exists (read at most once a second). Measured on 6.7.91 hosts
(findings/kwin-cursor-atomic-tests-2026-10-17.md): tests 5,500 -> ~290 a second at 4000 Hz, KWin's
pointer CPU -39..54 %, the cursor plane following the pointer.

